--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
redamon — https://github.com/samugit83/redamon  (MIT License)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Portions of the VIGIL-FUSION program adapt Python source from redamon (an
AI-powered agentic red-team framework). Adapted modules currently include the
untrusted-input framing, the deterministic scope guardrail, the transient-error
classifier + parameter self-heal, the non-authoritative cognition governors
(productivity scoring, the honesty audit, the uniform-response anomaly detector,
the tested-axes ledger, and the deep-think novelty guard — from redamon's
`productivity.py`), the MCP-server manifest layer (pydantic models, trust-tiered
`validate_servers`, secret redaction, and phase-view — from redamon's
`mcp_registry.py`, re-inverted to least-privilege / deny-by-default and
subordinated to VIGIL's WARDEN tier + conjunctive gate), the attack-chain graph
memory (the EvoGraph node/edge schema and the cross-session `query_prior_chains`
retrieval — from redamon's `chain_graph_writer.py`, reimplemented as a
projection-only, rebuildable read-model of the signed spine with a confirmed/lead
split, spine-hash provenance, and bi-temporal invalidate-not-delete so the graph
can never launder an unproven claim into a fact), and (in later phases) the live
MCP client binding, the AI-Gauntlet adapters, and the workspace/job tooling. The
bi-temporal (valid/invalid) memory model is a design reference from pentagi's
Graphiti, reimplemented in Python (see the pentagi note below).
These are adapted to VIGIL's sovereign, provable architecture (routed through the
deterministic oracle, the signed spine, and the governance gates; fail-open
defaults inverted to deny-by-default) rather than used verbatim.

