pentagi — https://github.com/vxcontrol/pentagi  (MIT License + EULA)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pentagi (an autonomous-pentest platform, written in Go) is used as DESIGN
REFERENCE ONLY. Its ideas (Chain-AST / Chain-Summary context engineering, the
mentor-supervision loop, bi-temporal knowledge-graph memory, the agent role
taxonomy, and one-identity observability) are reimplemented in Python for VIGIL;
its Go source, configuration, and documentation prose are NOT vendored. pentagi's
source is MIT-licensed but its EULA restricts use to lawful penetration testing
and bars redistribution of derivatives — reimplementing the ideas in original
Python avoids any derivative-of-source question while honoring the design credit.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AI-Gauntlet subprocess tools (later phases)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The offensive-LLM testing tools (garak — Apache-2.0; PyRIT — MIT; Giskard;
promptfoo) are invoked as SUBPROCESSES, not imported, so their dependencies and
licenses remain outside VIGIL's process. Each retains its own upstream license.
